# PWA install identity (issue #141) — staging is visually distinct from prod:
# different name + an amber theme color (prod is orange, dev violet) for
# at-a-glance clarity. The theme colour and the icon variant both match this env's
# amber-500 TopBar (src/lib/environment.ts), so bar, chrome, and home-screen icon
# agree — the theme colour used to be sky-blue, which matched nothing after the
# banner colours were assigned (sky is now the LOCAL bar).
VITE_PWA_NAME=Salt (Staging)
VITE_PWA_SHORT_NAME=Salt Stg
VITE_PWA_THEME_COLOR="#F59E0B"
VITE_PWA_ICON_PATH=/icons/staging

# VAPID public key for web-push cook-timer notifications (issue #544). Public
# by design (the private key is a CF secret). Per-environment DISTINCT keypair — a
# subscription minted under one project's public key is undeliverable by another's
# private key. Empty disables the notifications toggle. Generate the pair with
# `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys` and set the matching VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY secret
# + VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY env on the Cloud Functions side.
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=BBCdEvFDPQlH1ko2bpqXTR8u4W0NgYgbFHcGEP17ESXZzThR_3_yTwnb0JwkFRGECmqnYXDhe9Xts1h-0q6GMdM
